{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment is complete (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), leaving the most critical design question unresolved—whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest image-only model and serves as a direct, single-variable comparison to config_001, isolating the effect of modality while holding profile setting (single) and model complexity (no aggregation, no fusion) constant. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget with only one data point, the highest-priority uncertainty is whether image information is worth integrating at all. If image_only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion designs; if it performs substantially worse, it redirects effort toward improving the RNA pipeline (encoder choice, multiprofile aggregation). This experiment reduces the largest single source of uncertainty about the design space and avoids committing budget to multimodal or multiprofile variants before confirming the value of the second modality."
}

